  "definition": "The subiculum is a group of structures that forms the lowest part of the hippocampal formation, lying between the entorhinal cortex and the CA1 region of the hippocampus. It is involved in functions such as working memory, spatial processing, and regulation of the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis.",
